course: dictionary
lesson: 1976
title: Complicated: many parts, many steps
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Complicated means having many parts or steps, so it is hard to understand or do. A maths problem with lots of steps is complicated. Break it into small steps and do one step at a time.
explain: Complicated can also describe a situation with many problems or feelings mixed up. «New partners can be lovely, and that can feel complicated.» Here happy and worried feelings are tangled together, so the situation is hard to sort out.
explain: Look at the words around it to check the meaning. «Scientists say the story is more complicated than "wolves changed the rivers"» tells you the true story has more parts: bears, people and weather matter too. Ask yourself: how many parts are there?
fact: Complicated is an adjective. It describes a thing, such as a complicated problem or a complicated question.
fact: More complicated and most complicated compare how hard something is.
fact: Complicated is also the past form of the verb complicate, which means to make something harder to understand or do.
fact: Useful phrases: «it's complicated», «a complicated question», «too complicated».
fact: The opposite of complicated is simple, and headlines can make a complicated choice sound simple.
exercise: «The rules of the board game are complicated, with lots of steps.» What does complicated mean here? | *Having many parts or steps, so hard to do | Loud and noisy | Brightly coloured | Very short and easy
exercise: «New partners can be lovely, and that can feel complicated.» What makes this complicated? | *Happy and worried feelings are mixed up together | It is only about the weather | Everyone feels exactly the same | It has just one step
exercise: What is the best first step with a complicated maths problem? | Read the numbers backwards | *Break it into small steps and do one at a time | Guess the answer straight away | Skip it and never look at it again
test: «The story of the wolves is more complicated than the headline, because bears, people and weather also mattered.» What does complicated mean here? | *Having many parts that all matter | Funny and silly | Exactly the same as the headline | Very short and simple
test: Complicated is the past form of which verb? | Complain | *Complicate | Complicity | Compare
exam: Which sentence uses complicated correctly? | The sky was complicated and blue | Complicated is a sandwich I like | Yesterday I complicated my lunch | *The recipe has twenty steps, so it is very complicated
